        <p>Parish Churci.</p>
        <p>The will of the late Mr. F. G. Taylor, solicitor, contains certain private bequests. He also bequeath. £100„ which, after the death of his father, is to), invested and the annual income thereof paid to tit •• churchwardens of the Parish Church for the upkeep of the fabric of the church, but for no other purpose. Should the said church be taken from the Church of England, or out of its •de control and see, then the- income cf the trust fund may be changed to be so applied or wied for such other purpose. eccleriseticelly, in the parish of St. Elphin s, Warrington, as the rector of the said parish of Wartingtoo ahall then. direct. No rector or church-warden shall be a trust.e.</p>
