        <p>POIKETH V. SALE ALBION.</p>
        <p>Pent eth being thrown open through a re-plaverl cup tie, hurriedly arranged for Sale Albion to visit them. The game was well oonteeted all through, and the result a draw of one goal each was a true reflex of the game. Bowdon Vale two, St Vincent's one.</p>
        <p>SECOND DIVISION.</p>
        <p>ST. THOMAS (STOCKT,ON HRATH) v. OUGHTRINGTON</p>
        <p>AMATEURS.'</p>
        <p>At Stockton Heath. The visitors kicked off and scored as the result of a miskick by one of the home backs. The home team fought hard and evalized from penalty. Half-time: One goal each. L pon turning round play ruled f a awl eve-, the Amateurs again taking the lead with a capital goal only for the home team to equalise again from a penalty. About ten , minutes from time Oxen gave the borne custodian no chance with a lovely shot. Final: Oughtrington Amateurs, three; Stockton Heath St Thomas', two.</p>
        <p>SANKEY V. HOWLEY:</p>
        <p>At Luvely.lane. After good comb:nation Sankey opened the rcoring. Howley equalized from a penalty. Both defences were in capital trim, half-inure arriving with the score one goal each. Resuming, Sankey took up the running but found the visitorre defence firm, the goalkeeper in particular bringing off som4 smart saves. After 15 minutes' play Howley took the lead whilst shortly after they failed to convert a penalty, the home custodian bringing off a capital save. Changing the venue the home team applied reasure and equalized. No further scoring took place, the result hem); Sankey two,..flowley two. •</p>
