      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-10-21_WidnesExaminer_art0102" n="art0102">
        <head>PICTURES OF THE WEEK.</head>
        <p>PICTURES OF THE WEEK.</p>
        <p>SCOTTISH INVASION OF YARMOUTH.</p>
        <p>Thousands of Scottish fishermen and their womenfolk have again invaded Yarmouth for the herring fishing. This means the catching, curing and selling of about 500 million herrings annually. Our picture shows the Scotch lassies preparing and packing the fish in barrels for export, for more than two-thirds of the herrings landed are sent abroad to Germany, Holland and Russia.</p>
        <p>GENERAL LINUAN-HENG,</p>
        <p>This is a portrait of General Li-Yuan- Heng, who is in supreme command of the Rebel Forces in China. He first entered the Chinese Navy but subsequently trans- ferred to the Army. He was educated at Tientsin, and has visited England.</p>
