        <p>WAKE UP ENGLAND! 1913-IN GHEN T-1913 BELGIUM UNIVERSAL Arm INTERNATIONAL (APRIL TO OCTOBER) EXHIBITION. MAGNIFICENT GARDENS. TWENTY-FIVE COUNTRIES REPRESENTED. THOUSANDS OF ACRES COVERED BY PALATIAL BUILDINGS. FETES, AVIATION' AND EVERY KIND OF ATTRACTION. PRELIMINARY ANNOUNCEMENT. A great International nod Universal Exhibition will he held in Ghent, the Manchester of Belgium, in 1913. The object of this announcement is to urge the British Manufacturer to male a show worthy of our great Empire and to remember that the ancient battle grcund of Europe has MOW become the one neutral ground where the Inter- national Market can be made a success, as German and French al,ke will come to Ghent to see and buy our wares. The Exhibition Department of the Board of Trade has been approached to assure an adequate participation for England neat to the French section. Germany will have an admirable display and our Manufacturers most not neglect this opportunity. The Exhibitios will he bigger than the Bruseefe 1910 and the whole will be oat scale of magnificence hitherto unknown. It is tinder the direct Patronage of H.M. King Albert. An Office hes been specially opened at I, Southampton Row, WC., where all HiLirination and Booklets may be obtained. Send a P.C. to-day.</p>
